==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|hi}} [[नमस्कार]] / {{etyl|ur}} {{ur-Arab|[[نمسکار]]}} ''namaskār'' < {{etyl|sa}} [[नमस्कार]] ''namaskāra'', from ''namas'': "to bow", "[[obeisance]]" and ''kāra'': "action".

===Interjection===
'''namaskar'''

# respectful greetings

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{India}} The use of the [[greet]]ing in which you put your hands together and then [[bow]] slightly.

